From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:11:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 47/47] qwen27: a dense Qwen3.5 MTP head drafts on Metal

`--drafter DIR` now also takes a dense Qwen3.5 checkpoint's MTP head: a config
with one MTP layer (no dflash_config) and `mtp.safetensors` (the head's 15 BF16
tensors, as the cuda build reads it) or the checkpoint's shards, of which only
`mtp.*` loads. The head runs on the DFlash2 runtime as a second config kind: it
taps the embedding seam and the last layer through the same ring, absorbs each
committed row once its successor's embedding is known, and drafts a chain that
stops after the draft taking the chain probability under 0.5
(TF_QWEN27_MTP_CONFIDENCE) or at 8 drafts (TF_QWEN27_MTP_DEPTH). Its linears are
prepared to affine-4 at load. The startup line and /v1/models name the drafter
MTP.

M5 Ultra, Qwen3.5-9B q4 (MLX 4-bit, 65,536 x 4), served greedy, 256 tokens,
drafted / "draft": false, every reply token-identical:
1K 230 / 115 tok/s, 32K 172 / 102, code edit 441 / 116, re-quote 685 / 115,
story 215 / 115; 4 chats at 32K 145-176 / 88-100 tok/s a chat; acceptance
55-83%. HumanEval+ 164 and BFCL held 450 at --parallel 4: 614/614 replies
token-identical to the run without drafts (87.8 and 81.3), 76% and 71% of
drafts accepted. A fixed depth of 3 was the best fixed depth (1K 216, code edit
351); depth 8 without the cut drafted 26% acceptance and ran slower (1K 174).
